%% WeaveNYC — P2P Event Flow: Post to Match
%% Source: 07_P2P_Node_Design.md §4

sequenceDiagram
    participant E as Edge Node<br/>(User Mobile)
    participant A as Anchor Node<br/>(Community Org)
    participant C as Cloud Match<br/>(Match Service)
    participant D as Directory DB<br/>(Official Resources)

    E->>E: 1. Create Request locally
    E->>A: 2. post.published (opt-in sync)

    alt High-risk category (Childcare/Transport)
        A->>A: 3a. Add to review queue
        A-->>E: 3b. Notify: Awaiting Anchor review
        Note over A: Anchor manual review
        A->>A: 3c. moderation.decision (approve)
    else Low-risk category
        A->>A: 3a. Mark as matchable directly
    end

    A->>C: 4. Request match (candidate summary)
    C->>D: 5. Query resources (ZIP + category)
    D-->>C: 6. Return resource list
    C->>C: 7. Compute Top-3 action plans
    C-->>A: 8. Return match results
    A-->>E: 9. Push action plans (neighbor + official)
